  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q48-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "48",
    "prompt": "Let $\\displaystyle S_n=\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots+\\frac{n}{(n+1)!}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q48-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Simplify $\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{k!}-\\frac{1}{(k+1)!}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle \\frac{k}{(k+1)!}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{k!}-\\frac{1}{(k+1)!}&=\\frac{k+1}{(k+1)!}-\\frac{1}{(k+1)!}\\\\\\frac{1}{k!}-\\frac{1}{(k+1)!}&=\\frac{(k+1)-1}{(k+1)!}\\\\\\frac{1}{k!}-\\frac{1}{(k+1)!}&=\\frac{k}{(k+1)!}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q48-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence show that $\\displaystyle S_n=1-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p40-q48-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "S_n=1-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p40-q48-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use part (a) to express each summand as a difference; the intermediate terms cancel.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "From part (a),\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{1!}-\\frac{1}{2!}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{1}{2!}-\\frac{1}{3!}\\right)+\\cdots+\\left(\\frac{1}{n!}-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}\\right)\\\\S_n&=\\frac{1}{1!}-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}\\\\S_n&=1-\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q48-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the value of\n$$\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p40-q48-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p40-q48-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The remaining reciprocal factorial tends to zero.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "As $n$ increases without bound, $\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{(n+1)!}$ tends to $0$. Using part (b),\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots&=1-0\\\\\\frac{1}{2!}+\\frac{2}{3!}+\\frac{3}{4!}+\\cdots&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      }
    ]
  },
